Hi, RKWard in Ubuntu Intrepid Beta is currently broken: when you install
a *.deb package for intrepid from the ubuntu repositories (or compile it
yourselt the Debian way by taking sources either from ubuntu
repositories or from the sourceforge.net rkward debian repository) you
get Rkward without the Main menu and without the the "Welcome to RKward"
page.... Also, without the "Help" menu!

But if you compile it yourself with a simple sequence:

cd rkward_source_dir
cmake .
make
sudo make install

Rkward looks normal, only missing some icons...

I guess that means that there is an error in rkward sources, maybe
related to the former Kubuntu place to KDE4 packages...

Donatas Glodenis



